    "narrative": "With **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, **Josh Naylor**, and **James Wood** all sidelined by team off-days, our offensive ceiling is capped today, forcing us to rely on our secondary tier to anchor the 5x5 categories. **Zach McKinstry** represents our strongest play with a score of 57.26; his matchup against Rodriguez is the primary driver, as the opposing starter\u2019s 4.95 xERA suggests a prime environment for **Zach McKinstry** to capitalize on his recent momentum. While the platoon disadvantage against a righty knocks his efficiency down slightly, the SP skill profile is favorable enough to keep him well ahead of the replacement threshold. **Austin Riley** follows closely at 55.38, bolstered by a solid batting order position and a favorable park factor that helps offset the volatility of facing Tolle.\n\n**Seiya Suzuki** rounds out our active trio with a marginal 44.10 score, a result heavily suppressed by the elite matchup against Skenes. While the wind-out conditions at the park provide a slight +5% boost, the sub-3.00 xERA of Skenes\u2014paired with a high-efficiency catcher capable of stifling our SB-focused roster construction\u2014makes this a high-risk start. Among our non-active roster, names like **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, and **Brice Turang** were considered to provide depth, but none generated a higher projected efficiency than the starters listed. **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Tyler Soderstrom** remain on the bench as we look toward higher-probability matchups later in the week.\n\nWe are keeping a close watch on **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, and our deep prospect pool\u2014including **Carson Williams**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Kyle Karros**, **Alex Freeland**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte**\u2014to ensure our game caps are managed optimally during this off-day lull. The primary warning for today is the Skenes factor against **Seiya Suzuki**; if the pre-game reports indicate any shift in wind direction or lineup protection, we may see his efficiency drop even further toward our \"below floor\" threshold. We are playing for volume and stability today, hoping **Zach McKinstry** can provide the necessary spark to keep our AVG and R categories afloat.",
